<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kushan Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kushan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kushan Empire was a state founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuezhi">Yuezhi</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bactria">Bactria</a> that expanded into northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the first centuries CE. Its control of trade routes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, India, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> and the Roman world made it wealthy, and it patronised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a> and Gandharan art. Its decline left a political space in northern India in which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a> later rose.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kushan-empire.jpg" alt="Kushan Empire" width="320" height="296" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Map created from DEMIS Mapserver, which are public domain. Koba-chan. Reference: Schwartzberg Atlas, v. , p. 145. Map g · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Kushan_Empire.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
